,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
1,Tarjumo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarjumo_language,"Tarjumo, also known as Old Kanembu or Classical Kanembu, is a classical and sacred language created and used by Muslim scholars in the Kanem–Bornu Empire, located in the central Sahel.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
2,Tarjumo language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/tarjumo_language,"Written in Arabic script (Ajami) with innovations such as tone encoding on vowels—the earliest known in Arabic-script languages—Tarjumo reflects over a millennium of evolution from its Kanembu roots, distinguishing it phonologically and lexically from contemporary Saharan dialects around Lake Chad.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
3,"Tarjumo AI — Translation, Text-to-Speech & Speech Recognition ...",https://vambo.ai/languages/tarjumo,"What language family does Tarjumo belong to? Tarjumo (Tarjumo) belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family and is spoken in Nigeria, with approximately 3K speakers.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
4,Dunya – Top Saharan Music Hits Legend Sahara - YouTubeThe Rough Guide to the Music of the Sahara - Andy Morgan WritesSaharan songs and music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qO_WzaHUHbw,"Dunya – Top Saharan Music Hits 🎸Legend Sahara🔥 Feel the heat of the desert with Dunya – Top Saharan Music Hits! 🌍 From smooth Tuareg guitars to powerful tribal drums, this playlist... The Compagnie Jellouli & Gdih come from Erfoud, the capital of the Tafilalet, and they play a style of music known as al baldi, in which the elegance of Andalusian melodies are coupled with the searing intensity of Berber music from the Atlas, and the harrowing lyricism of popular malhoun poetry. May 25, 2025 · 🎼🎸Saharan Songs and Music A musical journey through the desert: hypnotic rhythms, Tuareg guitars, ancestral chants, and nomadic poetry.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
5,The Rough Guide to the Music of the Sahara - Andy Morgan Writes,https://www.andymorganwrites.com/the-rough-guide-to-the-music-of-the-sahara/,"The Compagnie Jellouli & Gdih come from Erfoud, the capital of the Tafilalet, and they play a style of music known as al baldi, in which the elegance of Andalusian melodies are coupled with the searing intensity of Berber music from the Atlas, and the harrowing lyricism of popular malhoun poetry.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
