7,Nilo-Saharan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/39/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..q1Sf4rd3drUq_qVbZh2jE_3soRxTIxU8lmX0apb_0eA,"Nilo-Saharan. Subgroup of 210 languages.Tarjumo txj, a language of Nigeria. Tebu 2.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
8,Nilo-Saharan Languages - SourceWatch,https://www.sourcewatch.org/index.php/Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan Languages are a family of 205 languages. The most common are Dholuo in Kenya and Kanuri in Nigeria with 3.5 million speakers each. The next largest, measured by number of speakers are: Kalenjin; Dinka, Lugbara; Lango; Maa; Acholi; Lendu; Ngambay...",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
9,Tarjumo language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Tarjumo_language,"Tarjumo, also known as Old Kanembu or Classical Kanembu, is a classical and sacred language created and used by Muslim scholars in the Kanem–Bornu Empire, located in the central Sahel.Language family. Nilo-Saharan.",Tarjumo,Nilo-Saharan
